Start the server:
npm start


Test these endpoints in Postman:
Method	URL	Expected result
GET	http://localhost:3000/health	200 OK
GET	http://localhost:3000/api/products	200 OK
GET	http://localhost:3000/api/products/1	200 OK
POST	http://localhost:3000/api/products	201 Created
PATCH	http://localhost:3000/api/products/1	200 OK
DELETE	http://localhost:3000/api/products/2	204 No Content
GET	http://localhost:3000/unknown	404 Not Found

For POST, select Body → raw → JSON and send:
{
  "name": "Monitor",
  "price": 7500
}


For PATCH, send:
{
  "price": 8200
}


A successful PATCH changes the price without replacing the product's name.

Note: the service currently stores products in an array, so data is temporary and will reset when the server restarts. A database connection is a good next step.
